     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 4, \"rationale\": \"The target can be reached through four attack paths that share no blockable steps, so at least one block is needed per path, giving a lower bound of 4. (1) phishing → configSecret → backupHost → mailArchive. (2) vpnGateway → containerHost → memoryDump → monitoringHost → dbReplica. (3) supplychain/exposedApi → iotDevice + kerberoast → apiToken → jumpHost → codeRepo. (4) wifiGuest → mailClient + sshKey → dbLogin → printServer → vaultRead. Blocking 4 steps is enough, so 4 is the minimum. One working set is printServer, jumpHost, monitoringHost and backupHost. Blocking printServer cuts vaultRead and hypervisor. Blocking jumpHost cuts codeRepo. Blocking monitoringHost cuts dbReplica, since hypervisor and printServer are already cut. Blocking backupHost cuts mailArchive, since secretsManager is still reachable but hypervisor is cut. Wait: secretsManager needs dbLogin AND apiToken, and both stay reachable, so mailArchive would still be reachable that way. A valid set is instead to block the four collection steps directly: codeRepo, dbReplica, mailArchive and vaultRead. That also gives 4.\"}"
    }
